However, this result is not guaranteed. Object's default hash codes can collide, in which case equals() may detect the duplicate even without the correct override.

Why does the duplicate appear?
The two Arun objects have identical registration numbers.

Their equals() method returns true.

However, they inherit hashCode() from the Object class.

Their identity-based hash codes can differ.

HashSet uses the hash code to select a bucket.

If the objects land in different buckets, HashSet may not compare them using equals().

Therefore, the same student can be stored twice.

