The object remains stored in the bucket determined by its original hash code. After changing regNo, HashSet searches using the new hash code and may look in a different bucket.

This can cause contains() to return false even though the object is physically present in the set.

Engineering lesson: Never modify fields involved in equals() or hashCode() while an object is stored in a HashSet.

