8. How HashSet works internally
HashSet internally uses a HashMap to store elements.

Interview Question - How Hashmap Works Internally? Unveiled Secrets
 
The process is:

HashSet receives a Student object.

It calls hashCode() to calculate the hash.

It identifies the appropriate bucket.

It checks existing objects in that bucket.

It calls equals() to determine whether the student already exists.

If an equal student exists, the new entry is rejected; otherwise, it is inserted.

Important: hashCode() identifies the likely bucket, while equals() confirms whether two objects are logically equal.

9. Alternative concept 1 – TreeSet with Comparator
Instead of HashSet, we can use TreeSet with a Comparator based on registration number.


