10. Alternative concept 2 – HashMap using registration number as key
Another approach is to store students in a HashMap, using the registration number as the key.


java
import java.util.HashMap;
import java.util.Map;

public class AttendanceMap {

    public static void main(String[] args) {

        Map<String, String> attendance = new HashMap<>();

        attendance.put("192311001", "Arun");
        attendance.put("192311002", "Divya");

        // Duplicate scan
        attendance.put("192311001", "Arun");

        System.out.println(
                "Unique students: " + attendance.size());
    }
}
Output:


text
Unique students: 2
Here, the registration number is the key. Since HashMap keys are unique, inserting the same key again replaces the existing value rather than creating another entry.

This is a convenient solution when registration numbers uniquely identify students.

