13. Final conclusion
The experiment demonstrates that overriding equals() alone is insufficient when using HashSet.

equals() determines whether two students are logically identical.

hashCode() helps HashSet locate the correct bucket.

Both methods must follow the Java contract.

Fields used for equality and hashing should preferably be immutable.

TreeSet is suitable when sorted attendance records are required.

HashMap is suitable when registration numbers can directly serve as unique keys.

Final recommendation: For college fest attendance de-duplication, use HashSet<Student> with correctly overridden equals() and hashCode(), based on the immutable registration number.

This provides average 
O(1)
O(1) insertion and lookup while ensuring duplicate student scans are rejected
